# RESONA UI SPEC

## 0. Document purpose

This document defines the visual, interaction, and component specification for **RESONA**, a web-based interactive music app where voice, touch, melody, and synced users become visual matter.

This document should be used together with the reference images in:

```txt
docs/design/references/01-solo-glass.png
docs/design/references/02-capture-glass.png
docs/design/references/03-merge-room.png
docs/design/references/04-liquid-mode.png
```

The first implementation goal is to reproduce the visual and interaction language of these images as a static or semi-interactive React/Next.js prototype.

Real audio processing, microphone input, pitch detection, recording, and WebSocket syncing should be added only after the UI foundation is close to the references.

---

# 1. Product concept

## 1.1 One-sentence definition

**RESONA is an interactive web music app where voice and touch are transformed into instrument sounds, melodic traces, loops, and visual matter.**

## 1.2 Core experience

RESONA should feel like:

* You can touch sound.
* Your voice becomes a visual object.
* A melody becomes a glowing trace.
* A captured sound becomes an orbiting loop.
* Multiple people merge into one shared resonant space.
* The UI material changes with the sound material.

## 1.3 What RESONA is not

RESONA is not:

* a traditional DAW
* a piano-roll editor
* a mixer
* a waveform editor
* a generic audio visualizer
* a flat SaaS dashboard
* a complicated music production tool

It should not look like Ableton, GarageBand, FL Studio, or a normal recording app.

RESONA is closer to a **touchable musical organism** or **sound-as-material interface**.

