## 5.2 Capture screen

Reference:

```txt
docs/design/references/02-capture-glass.png
```

### Purpose

The state where RESONA is listening, tracing a melody, and creating loops.

### Header

Title:

```txt
RESONA
```

Subtitle:

```txt
Tracing your melody.
```

### Main visual

The Glass Matter orb remains central, but now includes active recording feedback:

* magenta/violet recording ring
* glowing circular progress arc
* pitch trace line crossing the orb
* waveform accents on left and right
* small nodes along the pitch path
* more active glow than Solo state

### Timer

Display:

```txt
● 00:08
```

The dot should be magenta/red-violet.
The timer should be large, calm, and centered.

### Status text

```txt
Listening and shaping your melody
```

### Loop chips

Show loop chips under the timer:

```txt
LOOPS

Loop 01  00:07  ×
Loop 02  00:05  ×
＋
```

Loop chips are glassmorphic rounded pills.

### Matter selector

Glass remains selected.

### Primary actions

Capture button is active and brighter.
Merge remains available but secondary.

### Required state data

```ts
type CaptureState = {
  mode: "capture";
  matter: "glass";
  isRecording: true;
  elapsedSeconds: number;
  loops: Array<{
    id: string;
    name: string;
    durationSeconds: number;
    color: "blue" | "purple" | "magenta";
  }>;
};
```

