# 11. Implementation phases

## Phase 0.1: Static UI

Goal:

Recreate the four reference states visually.

Must include:

* Solo Glass
* Capture Glass
* Merge Room
* Liquid Mode
* state changes using buttons
* no real audio
* no networking
* no storage

## Phase 0.2: Interactive UI mock

Add:

* pointer interactions
* animated level meter
* mock recording timer
* loop chip add/remove
* animated resonance meter
* matter transitions

## Phase 0.3: Local audio

Add:

* microphone permission
* level detection
* basic pitch detection
* voice-to-synth mapping
* local capture mock

## Phase 0.4: Real capture and loop

Add:

* recording
* back capture
* loop creation
* loop playback
* orbit visualization

## Phase 0.5: Merge room

Add:

* WebSocket room
* mock synchronized users
* shared resonance state
* basic real-time input sharing

---

# 12. First prototype acceptance criteria

The first prototype is acceptable when:

* the screen immediately feels like the reference images
* the app is clearly recognizable as RESONA
* the background, glow, orb, panels, and buttons match the premium blue/purple glassmorphism direction
* Solo / Capture / Merge / Liquid states are visually distinct
* the UI does not feel like a generic dashboard
* the UI does not feel like a normal audio recorder
* the controls are simple and readable
* the component structure is clean and ready for audio features later

The first prototype is not acceptable if:

* it looks like a standard SaaS app
* it is too flat
* it uses too many sliders
* it looks like a DAW
* the central visual object is weak
* the buttons dominate too much
* the app feels cluttered
* there is no sense that sound becomes matter

